From: Hazel Smith <hazel@hazelesque.uk>
Subject: Makefile: set libc-mimalloc-introspectable.so.1 SONAME at link time

We need libc.so's DT_SONAME to advertise the variant name so
binaries linked against this variant DT_NEED that name (and
can't silently fall back to system libc).

The previous approach used `patchelf --set-soname` in post_install
after the upstream link finished.  That worked SONAME-wise but
left the binary segfaulting on direct invocation as a loader
(`ld-musl-mimalloc-introspectable-x86_64.so.1 --version`).
Inspection showed the variant had 11 program headers vs vanilla
musl's 10, with an extra GNU_EH_FRAME — patchelf had relocated
data and added segments to fit the longer SONAME string, which
broke musl's static-PIE startup path that's sensitive to ELF
layout.

Setting the SONAME at link time instead gives a clean ELF with
the same layout as vanilla.  Also drops patchelf as a
hostmakedepend.

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -170,7 +170,7 @@ obj/%.lo: $(srcdir)/%.c $(GENH) $(IMPH)

 lib/libc.so: $(LOBJS) $(LDSO_OBJS) $(EXTRA_OBJ)
 	$(CC) $(CFLAGS_ALL) $(LDFLAGS_ALL) -nostdlib -shared \
-	-Wl,-e,_dlstart -o $@ $(LOBJS) $(LDSO_OBJS) $(LIBCC)
+	-Wl,-e,_dlstart -Wl,-soname=libc-mimalloc-introspectable.so.1 -o $@ $(LOBJS) $(LDSO_OBJS) $(LIBCC)

 lib/libc.a: $(AOBJS) $(EXTRA_OBJ)
 	rm -f $@
